WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:01.650
(horns honking)
(crowd chattering)

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.620
- [Jared] Turkey is headed to
a runoff election on May 28th.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.037
(Recep speaking in foreign language)

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:17.586
(Kemal speaking in foreign language)

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.140
- What happens in this election
will have enormous stakes,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.540
both for Turkey and for
the rest of the world.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.210
Turkey is a member of
NATO, a member of the G20,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.070
one of the world's largest economies.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.520
It's also a country that has
a central geopolitical role

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.480
in the Middle East,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.970
and in the war between Russia and Ukraine.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.770
Erdogan is one of the only world leaders

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.910
who speaks regularly

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.010
with Russia's president, Vladimir Putin,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.683
making him an important
channel into the Kremlin.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.290
President Erdogan is facing a number

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.780
of challenges to his reelection.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.910
Turkey has been in a currency crisis

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.310
over the last two plus years

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.590
in part due to his own economic decisions

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.020
in which he has pressured the central bank

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.160
into cutting interest rates

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.560
in spite of Turkey's
high rate of inflation.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.780
It's caused living standards to unravel.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.850
The rising costs of food, of housing,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.000
of medicine has really
narrowed Erdogan's power base

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.840
and turned some people who used
to vote for him against him.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.060
Another challenge is
the devastation caused

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.410
by the earthquakes that shook
Turkey and Syria in February.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.980
It killed more than 56,000 people.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.750
People living in the earthquake zone said

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.790
that they were basically left alone

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.680
and that state institutions,

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.870
including the emergency
services, the police

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.810
and the army were slow to
arrive, leaving thousands

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.460
of people underneath the
rubble waiting to be rescued.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.960
(Mehmet speaking in foreign language)

00:01:56.586 --> 00:01:57.419
On the other hand,

00:01:57.419 --> 00:02:00.360
Kemal Kilicdaroglu is
the long-serving leader

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.340
of Turkey's largest opposition party,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.470
the Republican People's Party.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.170
If Kilicdaroglu wins, it
would be a historic victory

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.410
for Turkey's opposition and
it would really breathe life

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.530
into democratic
institutions here in Turkey.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.590
He's been a fixture in
Turkish politics for decades.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.780
He has been leading the Turkish opposition

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.400
over the last decade.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.500
His profile as a kind

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.253
of elder statesman positions
himself as anti-Erdogan.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.720
He likes to say that he doesn't
use polarizing language.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.460
At the same time, he's promising

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.640
to accelerate Turkey's clamp down

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.240
on immigrants promising to push millions

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.243
of Syrian and Afghan
refugees out of the country.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.970
Over the last 20 years,
Erdogan has made himself

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.520
into Turkey's most powerful
leader in a century.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.430
And if he's brought down
through Democratic means,

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.230
that could inspire hope

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.449
that other countries could do the same.

00:02:57.449 --> 00:03:00.116
(pensive music)

